{"_id":"006DBrvIMFuio3AR","name":"Deck Chest Trap","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:deck-chest-trap","level":5,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR III p. 374","description":"A Deck Chest Trap can disguise itself as a variety of ordinary furniture, such as bookcases, doors, beds, etc. It can move its strong arms and two small legs in and out at will.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arms","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":39,"max":39},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry/15/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It can mimic treasure chests, furniture, and doors. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 15, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster can be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Deck Chest Trap can make two Smash attacks each round.\nThey may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Capture","description":"If both Smash attacks from [ ► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack] hit the target, the target becomes entangled by Deck Chest Trap. The target will not be able to move, and from the next round on, any attack from this monster to the entangled target will automatically hit.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Magical Wood (200G/Gold Green A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Premium Magical Wood (500G/Gold Green A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Deck Chest Trap","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"01jxmNqyYq8kkrkq","name":"Alchemy Tooth","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:alchemy-tooth","level":10,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Ruins, Cave","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18(Crawling)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR III p. 378","description":"This particular construct has a bacterium that causes the Golden Disease, which eventually turns a person's entire body into gold. While someone with the Golden Disease eventually dies and stiffens into a golden statue, their entire body is not actually gold. However, unscrupulous salesmen will attempt to sell these bodies as golden statues in hopes of duping people out of their hard-earned money.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":83,"max":83},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Golden Disease/15 (22)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Bite attack hits, it infects the target with a &quot;Golden Disease&quot; disease.\nTarget immediately receives a 2d disease magic damage and an additional 1d disease magic damage at the end of each round (no additional checks are needed in that case).\nAs the disease deals damage, golden spots spread from the wound, eventually turning the whole body gold. If the target dies from this disease, after 24 hours, their entire body is stiff gold, and the character cannot be resurrected.\nThe Golden Serum earned from defeating an Alchemy Tooth can be used to cure this disease (but not the HP lost). If taken in advance, it will prevent the character from catching this disease for up to 24 hours.\nA Major Action is needed to take Golden Serum."},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If an Alchemy Tooth successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Golden Serum (300G/Gold A) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Golden Scales (600G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Alchemy Tooth","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"2l0u2ESUBaeTo98b","name":"Rainbow Rainmaker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rainbow-rainmaker","level":9,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"High altitudes","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20 (Floating)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 128","description":"This is a Construct that has been sighted near the Northern Fang Mountain range in the Dorden region. It constantly floats high in the sky and is indistinguishable from clouds from a distance.\n\nThere are reports of incidents where it very rarely appears close to the ground, causing rainbow-colored rain or localized hailstorms.\n\nIt is said to have been created by magicians during the Magic Civilization Period for entertainment purposes, but there are few records in literature, and it's largely unknown why it was created or what its purpose was.\n\nThe &quot;Rainbow Magic Power&quot; used in its core is believed to utilize the pinnacle of Magic Civilization Period technology and is sought after by some researchers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Core)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":104,"max":104},"mp":{"value":66,"max":66}},{"style":"Stone (Cloud)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":31,"max":31}},{"style":"Stone (Cloud)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":91,"max":91},"mp":{"value":31,"max":31}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity, ◯Water/Ice Immunity, ◯Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"◯Cloud Body","description":"It cannot be critically hit by bladed weapons and treats attacks from blunt weapons as having 5 points of Defense higher."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"When the HP of the Core falls to 0 or less while any of the Clouds has HP above 0, the loot item &quot;Rainbow Magic Power&quot; will be lost."},{"title":"►Rainbow Rain/Can't","description":"Causes rainbow-colored rain to fall on itself and the surrounding area. Targets within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;All Area (30m radius/All)&quot; roll 1d to determine the effect received from the rain according to the &quot;Rainbow Rain Effect Determination Table&quot; below.\nAll effects in the table are treated as Poison type with a Success Value of 20.\nRainbow Rain Effect Determination Table\n1d | Effect Name | Effect Details |\n1 | Rain of Despair | Immediately take &quot;1d+1&quot; points of fixed damage to both HP and MP. |\n2 | Blinding Rain | Treated as blind for 10 seconds (1 round). |\n3 | Chilling Rain | For 10 seconds (1 round), receive an additional +3 points of damage when taking physical or magical damage of the &quot;Water/Ice&quot; type. |\n4 | Clinging Rain | For 10 seconds (1 round), receive a -2 penalty to Evasion checks, Fortitude, and Willpower. |\n5 | Delicious Rain | Immediately recover &quot;2d&quot; points of HP, but unable to move or take Major Actions. |\n6 | Mana Rain | For 10 seconds (1 round), all Magic Power is increased by +2, but all skill check rolls of 4 or less are treated as automatic failures. |"},{"title":"Cloud","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = Impossible・Impossible","description":"Overflowing clouds block attacks. The Core section cannot be targeted by Melee or Ranged Attacks. This effect is lost when the HP of one or more Cloud sections becomes 0 or less."},{"title":"►Hail / 12 (19) / Willpower / Half","description":"Attacks by causing hail to fall on the target's head. Deals 2d+10 points of Water/Ice magic damage to targets in &quot;1 area (4m radius)/10&quot; within &quot;Range: 2(30m).&quot;\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns, and if any Cloud section uses it, all other Cloud sections cannot use it."},{"title":"►Ice Spike / 12 (19) / Evasion check / Negates","description":"Attacks by thrusting an ice spike from within the cloud. Deals 2d+12 points of Water/Ice physical damage to 1 target character within &quot;Range: 1(10m).&quot;"}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Rainbow Magic Power (6,000G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Unmeltable Hail (1,700G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rainbow Rainmaker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3O2O1ZGy6QSMwAGa","name":"Carnage Table","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:carnage-table","level":10,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"4 (21)","willpower":"3 (20)","source":"CR II p. 382","description":"This magical device was created as a &quot;dream food table&quot; in the Magic Civilization Period. Underneath the four-legged rectangular table, storage is installed to store foodstuffs. The table is equipped with a long, thin arm that serves the food to the table.\n\nMany of those that remain today have malfunctioned. It restrains those seated and does not release them until all the food that appears endlessly has been consumed. Those who try to force their way out or harm them are punished with serving arms and stored in the storage as food for the next visitor. Malfunctioning storage will also most likely lose its ability to keep food fresh.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Table)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":98,"max":98},"mp":{"value":30,"max":30}},{"style":"Tableware (Serving Arms)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":30,"max":30}},{"style":"Tableware (Serving Arms)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":30,"max":30}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Table","description":""},{"title":"► Food Temptation/13 (20)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"Puts out a meal that looks attractive on the table and lures the target with the look and smell of the food.\nAll the characters in the same position (coordinates or area) as the storage section will eat the food on the table on failed resistance check.\nAfter that, characters at the end of each turn of the Table section will receive 3 Poison magic damage (9 maximum damage total). When Table section HP becomes 0 or less, it disappears."},{"title":"► Public Kitchen/13 (20)/Willpower/Negates","description":"The storage area under the dining table temporarily becomes transparent and visible, giving a graphic view of the food being prepared.\nWith &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 2-3 areas (10m Radius)/All,&quot; targets cannot take Minor Actions for 10 seconds (1 round) (Major Action and Active Combat Feats can still be declared). For the same duration receiving HP or MP recovery effects, the amount of recovery will be reduced by half (rounded up)."},{"title":"Serving Arms","description":""},{"title":"► Rampant Dishes/15 (22)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Throws many dishes. The effect will cause a 2d+12 physical damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot; at &quot;Range /Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot; and will consume 10 MP."},{"title":"► Forced Seating/13 (20)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The character is forcibly seated at the dining table. The seated character automatically fails the Fortitude and Willpower check for the ability used by the Table section without rolling any dice."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • Impossible","description":"Its body hinders attacks.\nThe Table section cannot be attacked, whether melee or ranged. This effect disappears when any of the Serving Arms falls to 0 HP or lower."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Silverware (50G/Black White B) x 2d"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Memento (1,000G/White S)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Enchanted Object (2,000G/Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Carnage Table","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"57cvNQizVUp0A5rE","name":"Flying Hoop","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:flying-hoop","level":5,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 127","description":"This Construct is found among ruins from the Magic Civilization Period. It consists of thin iron rods, approximately 2m in diameter, that are connected to form a floating horizontal ring. The ring rotates on its own axis while remaining in a horizontal position. Positioned on top of the ring are a pair of eyes floating at a height of around 50cm. There is no physical link between the ring and the eyes; they are believed to be magically connected.\n\nSimilar to other Constructs, it appears to have served as a guardian, protecting places and belongings by attacking and eliminating anyone who approaches it.\n\nWhen defeated, it sometimes leaves behind magic iron rings that continue spinning. These rings are highly sought after and sold at a premium as rare and valuable items, although they are not yet used as materials for special products.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":35,"max":35},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨Fly Around","description":"A Flying Hoop can attempt a Slam attack on any and all characters within &quot;Range: Touch.&quot;\nEach character designated as a target of this attack rolls 1d. If the roll is &quot;1-3,&quot; the character is attacked and must make an Evasion check. If the roll is &quot;4-6,&quot; the character is automatically out of the route of the Slam and does not need to perform an Evasion check. This 1d roll is subject to modifications that affect the check whether the character is involved in an &quot;Area: Line/Breakthrough,&quot; such as Lucky Feathers ."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magic Iron Ring (2,500G/Gold Black S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Flying Hoop","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5NbQYOimgxdP1KIJ","name":"Mithril Golem","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mithril-golem","level":20,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":19,"weakness":25,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"26 (33)","willpower":"25 (32)","source":"CR III p. 382","description":"A humanoid golem created entirely out of the magical metal mithril, the Mithril Golem is a 10m tall behemoth. However, the Mithril Golem is one of the most dangerous monsters known to exist in the entirety of Raxia, so defeating one and taking the treasure it guards is much easier said than done.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist (Upper Body)","accuracy":"26 (33)","damage":"2d+26","evasion":"23 (30)","defense":30,"hp":{"value":204,"max":204},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Fist (Upper Body)","accuracy":"26 (33)","damage":"2d+26","evasion":"23 (30)","defense":30,"hp":{"value":204,"max":204},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Kick (Lower Body)","accuracy":"24 (31)","damage":"2d+28","evasion":"22 (29)","defense":30,"hp":{"value":228,"max":228},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Kick (Lower Body)","accuracy":"24 (31)","damage":"2d+28","evasion":"22 (29)","defense":30,"hp":{"value":228,"max":228},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Knowledge = Conjurer Class","description":"Those with Conjurer will automatically succeed in the Monster Knowledge check for this monster. But they still must roll to know its weak point."},{"title":"◯ Mithril Body","description":"The Mithril Golem is immune to criticals from edged weapons and all Magic damage. The Mithril Golem's melee attacks are treated as silver weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Upper Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Improved Aimed Attack","description":"When attacking, the Mithril Golem can gain a +4 bonus to Accuracy but receives a -8 penalty for damage dealt."},{"title":"► Glowing Fists","description":"Wraps its fists with magical light for 10 seconds (1 round), and the damage it generates in a melee attack becomes energy magic damage."},{"title":"Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"► Simultaneous Attack","description":"A Mithril Golem's Kick attacks all characters in the same position."},{"title":"► Earthshaker/25 (32)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The Mithril Golem shakes the ground, and those who fail to resist immediately fall prone."},{"title":"◯ Balance Loss","description":"If the HP of any Lower Body section is reduced to 0 or less, the remaining Lower Body sections lose their [ ► Earthshaker] and [ ► Simultaneous Attack] abilities."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"Upper Body sections cannot be attacked in melee. Against any ranged attacks, Upper Body sections receive a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nThis effect disappears when all Lower Body sections fall to 0 HP or lower."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S) x 2d"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Pure Mithril (8,800G/Gold S) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mithril Golem","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7WwuJeLJK4Mqa0iO","name":"Ghast Queen","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast-queen","level":10,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"30/-","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"This is a bloated queen of Ghasts who has engulfed other Ghasts. Although she has no unique skills, she has acquired a formidable fighting ability and is a considerable threat to any visitor to her ruins.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arm","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":107,"max":107},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Dense Magic Jewel (700G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Glittering Magic Stone (1,300G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast Queen","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"84tfi03WGve9gYEQ","name":"Chest Mimic","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:chest-mimic","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"-/-","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"This Construct resembles a treasure chest and has the ability to move its powerful arms and small legs in and out as it pleases. There is speculation that it may be a type of Golem that was created in the past, but there is no certainty.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arm","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":25,"max":25},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry / 12 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"It disguises itself as a treasure chest. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with Target Number 12, and if it fails, they will be surprised. Mimicry will automatically end once the monster starts to act."},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"Attacks twice with Arms the same target."},{"title":"◯ Capture","description":"If both [ ► Double Attack] hit the target, the target is entangled. The target cannot move, and from the next round, attacks from this monster to the target will automatically hit the target.\nWhen the target attempts to escape, it should follow de-bonding rules (see ML, p. 71)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 11","loot":"Magical Wood (200G/Red Green A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Premium Magical Wood (500G/Red Green A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Chest Mimic","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"9H264ewk2OlafxcR","name":"Core Imitator","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:core-imitator","level":4,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/13(Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"AB, p. 103","description":"This is a Construct that mimics an Abyss Core. It was created as a trap by magicians who made their home in the Shallow Abyss, such as Quepala . Documented cases are concentrated within Shallows, with very few instances discovered outside.\n\nWhile it attacks using mimicry, if defeated within the Shallow, it generates an exit to lure intruders outside. Those who fail to see through its true nature fall into this trap and end up leaving the Shallow prematurely.\n\nWhen defeated, it drops an Abyss Shard. This too is part of its disguise. A cautious adventurer might grow suspicious of the small quantity.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sword","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"&#32;","defense":5,"hp":{"value":5,"max":5},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Mimicry / 13 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"Mimics an Abyss Core. While Mimicry is active, Monster Knowledge checks cannot be performed against this monster. If approached carelessly, perform a Danger Sense check with a target value of 13; if failed, you will be caught off guard. Mimicry automatically deactivates when actions begin.\nThe monster still responds to magic such as [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Core Imitator receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the result of 2d for damage determination is 10 or higher, increase the damage by an additional +6 points."},{"title":"◯Exit Generation","description":"When this monster is defeated while in the Shallow Abyss, it tears through space to generate a temporary escape route from the Shallow. The exit exists for only one hour before closing. Unlike when the Abyss Core is actually destroyed, the Shallow does not collapse, nor are its contents forcibly teleported to other locations."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Core Imitator","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"EHGXTGQgGHrrYpha","name":"Sinker House","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sinker-house","level":8,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"5 (Crawling)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 380","description":"A monster that mimics a tiny traveler's hut, room, or other such building, the Sinker House is deceptively dangerous. Fitting in an area usually around 5m in height, width, and depth, the Sinker House can be attacked through the floor or walls. The house can create a sizeable conical drill to attack the inhabitants, changing the floor to make it more dangerous for the inhabitants all the while.\n\nWhile the Sinker House is often seen as a small hut, it can appear as any indoor and outdoor room to trap victims inside. However, these rooms do seem to be slightly distorted, and this distortion can give away the Sinker House's mimicry.\n\nAdditionally, Gargoyles and other flying creatures find the interior quite welcoming, making it all the more dangerous for unaware adventurers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Drill","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":70,"max":70},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry/18/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It can mimic rooms. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 18, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster can be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"► Triple Attack","description":"Sinker House can attack the same target with three attacks."},{"title":"⏩ Room Rotation","description":"Sinker House can flip itself 180 degrees, swapping the floor and ceiling. All non-flying characters will fall 5m (taking fall damage) and fall prone.\nThis unique skill can only be used once per round and cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ Floor Change","description":"Sinker House changes the floor of the room to one of the following states. This unique skill can be used only once per round.\nSoftening: The Sinker House can make the floor soft and challenging to walk on. Characters standing on the floor will receive a -2 penalty for Evasion, but any character falling on a softened floor will take no damage.\nIgnition/10 (17)/Willpower/Half: The Sinker House sets the floor on fire, dealing 2d-2 fire magic damage to all characters standing on it.\nFreezing: The floor becomes icy and slippery. All characters on the floor receive a -2 penalty on their Accuracy checks. In addition, at the end of their turn, they must make check 2d + Adventurer Level + Agility modifier with target number 13, falling prone if they fail this check."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Premium Magical Wood (500G/Gold Green A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Luxury Magical Wood (3,600G/Gold Green S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sinker House","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HS83KoSa38EUqvd8","name":"Ghast","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast","level":1,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Ruins","reputation":5,"weakness":10,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"CR I p. 420","description":"A lost soul bound to a shadow, Ghasts live a sorry existence. Originally thought to have been created during the Magic Civilization period, Ghasts continue to spawn and thrive today in the shadows of civilization. The reason for their creation has been forgotten to time, though their extremely gaunt frame and pitch-black body are difficult to forget. Ghasts are not known to be solitary, so if one is seen, others are sure to follow.\n\nOccasionally, Ghasts will be summoned by Barbarous carrying magical stones. These stones are given to the regular members by Drakes , who keep close the secret of manufacturing.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Smash","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":14,"max":14},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HfSEh9XLePRoGNqk","name":"Magic Pot","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:magic-pot","level":8,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"18 (Jumping)/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"BM","description":"This Construct was created during the Magic Civilization Period. At first glance, it appears to be a large urn, but inside it lives a 60-centimeter-long, dark-skinned Ogre-like construct with a gaping mouth and eyes. Inside, the construct hides in the jar to skillfully fend off attacks.\n\nThe pot has the ability to move by bouncing and rolling.\n\nThe Construct was created to serve as a secret guardian among its owner's furnishings, and those that remain in the labyrinths and ruins today will attack intruders in an attempt to fulfill that role.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":70,"max":70},"mp":{"value":40,"max":40}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Pot Shot","description":"The attack is made by something radiating or being fired from the pot's mouth.\nThere are the following types of attacks, which are performed at random. The target of an attack, or the targets of an &quot;Area: Line &quot; attack, are selected at random from among the enemies within range.\nFire Storm / 10 (17) / Willpower / Half: Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; spreads fire over &quot;1 area (6m Radius) / 20&quot;. Targets are dealt &quot;2d+10&quot; Fire magic damage.\nDischarge / 10 (17) / Willpower / Half: Within &quot;Range / Area: 2 (20m) / Line &quot; fires a lightning bolt, dealing &quot;2d+10&quot; Lightning magic damage to targets.\nAcid Spray / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Half: Within &quot;Range / Area: 2 (30m) / Shot ,&quot; spits acid on &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, dealing target &quot;2d+12&quot; Poison magic damage.\nIron Ball Shot / 9 (16) / Evasion / Negates: Within &quot;Range / Area: 2 (20m) / Line &quot; shoots an iron ball. Deals 2d+12 physical damage to the target, and the target falls prone.\nLong Arm Attack / 11 (18) / Evasion / Negates: Attacks with Claws &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot;. Long Arms jumping out of the jar can ignore any skirmish area.\nClaws Attack / 11 (18) / Evasion check / Negates: Within &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; attacks &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with its Claws (same as regular melee attack).\nWhich attack will be made is random, but predictable if the PC has successfully completed a Monster Knowledge check. The GM should determine immediately after the attack what the &quot;next attack&quot; will be and tell the players (only the first attack is unpredictable, and they do not know the target of each attack)."},{"title":"◯ Ceramic Body","description":"A Magic Pot is immune to criticals from edged weapons and all magic damage, with the exception of Energy-type damage."},{"title":"◯ Mana Coating","description":"Any magic damage the Magic Pot suffers is reduced by -3."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Magical Ceramic Shards (250G/Gold Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Dense Magic Jewel (700G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Magic Stones (1,900G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Magic Pot","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"IZ9b7mI1KL0d9Qvu","name":"Diadema","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diadema","level":4,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Daemonic","habitat":"Shallow","reputation":11,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Floating)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"BM","description":"A Diadema is a construct that resembles a small Shallow Abyss. It appears as a sphere of blurred blackness, approximately 50 cm in size.\n\nUsing Summoning Arts to a limited extent, it attacks by temporarily manifesting a body part, such as Daemon's arms, from its center.\n\nToday, it is recognized as a failed or residual product of Daemon research during the Magic Civilization Period.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arm","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":24,"max":24}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Attitude Control","description":"It cannot fall prone under any effect."},{"title":"► Summoning Arts 4 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Daemon's Blood (100G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diadema","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KgyoX5YXCgBVHygZ","name":"Exceed Disaster","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:exceed-disaster","level":11,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"-/20(Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"CR III p. 378","description":"This is a self-sustaining sword created by a sorcerer who studied Swords of Genesis during the Magic Civilization Period as the result of their research. It is about 5 meters long.\n\nSwords of Genesis have been studied from various aspects, but the monstrosity that we see here was created to reproduce its performance and power and has survived to the present day. The size of the sword is also too large to be handled by a humanoid.\n\nStrictly speaking, it's not a magic sword but a Construct in the shape of a sword, but it seems that some of the research results were able to reproduce part of the secret of Swords of Genesis.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sword (Sword)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":90,"max":90},"mp":{"value":34,"max":34}},{"style":"Swing (Handle)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":75,"max":75},"mp":{"value":28,"max":28}},{"style":"Slam (Sheath)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":80,"max":80},"mp":{"value":68,"max":68}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"This monster receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Sword","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mithril Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons and all Magic damage. Sword section melee attacks are treated as silver weapons."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"It can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"🗨 Lethal Strike II","description":"The 2d roll of damage decision is increased by +1. At risk, he takes a -1 penalty to its Evasion check."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides. Accuracy checks are made at once, and damage is determined individually. If this ability is declared with [ 🗨 Power Strike II] or [ 🗨 Lethal Strike II], the damage will be changed only for one target."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +8 points. When declaring [ 🗨 Lethal Strike II], this ability is triggered when the modified roll is 10 (the original roll was 9) or more."},{"title":"Handle","description":""},{"title":"◯ Careful Balance","description":"The well-balanced and carefully crafted handle helps to move the sword blade. The Sword section has the ability of [ ◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times]. This ability is lost when the HP of the Handle section becomes 0 or less."},{"title":"► Gale Breath/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"The dragon on the handle spits torrent from the dragon's mouth and deals 2d+l1 wind magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius)/5&quot; at &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot;.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Sheath","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 10 Level/Magic Power 12 (19)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Universal Metamagic ]."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Gold Thread Decoration (800G/Gold White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Gold and Silver Decoration (1,800G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Jewelry Decoration (7,800G/Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Exceed Disaster","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Mdg3dDSQKafpDizT","name":"Culvert Slime","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:culvert-slime","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"8 (Flowing)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"KF","description":"This is a Mucus construct that can grow up to 1 meter long. It inhabits places where the smell of decay is present, and is believed to have been created to clean up dirty areas such as dark walls and sewers. It absorbs anything it comes into contact with and takes it into its body, giving it a black and muddy appearance like sludge. When discovered, it is typically exterminated by burning it with fire.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Soft Body","description":"Blunt weapons treat the Defense of Culvert Slime as 5 points higher."},{"title":"◯ Mucus of Disease/4 (11)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"A target hit by a Slam has its Dexterity and Agility reduced by -2 points. For monster characters, roll 1d. It has its Accuracy check reduced by 1d if the roll is &quot;1-3&quot; and its Evasive check reduced by -1 point if the roll is &quot;4-6&quot;.\nThis effect is Disease type and lasts until it is removed."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Tainted Mucus (80G/Red B)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Soulscarred Mucus (440G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Culvert Slime","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"MrkY838tVriFi5Wu","name":"Blob","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:blob","level":4,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Labyrinths","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"3","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 114","description":"A Blob is a translucent, light-green jelly that is highly acidic to the point of being able to dissolve metal. Originally the result of a magical experiment gone wrong, it now mindlessly divides itself to increase its population. Occasionally, an expiring Blob will release a harmless miniature version of itself without the acidity. This &quot;mini-Blob&quot; can be taken as a pet.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Engulf / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Slam attack hits, the Blob engulfs the target into its body. The target cannot move or perform any Major Actions and suffers 2d+1 magic damage at the end of each of the monster's turns.\nAn engulfed target can only perform one Fortitude Check on its turn, and if it succeeds, it can escape. After this check, the target's turn ends immediately, regardless of the result."},{"title":"◯ Soft Body","description":"Bludgeoning weapons treat the Defense of Blob section as 5 points higher. Also, Throw or similar attacks deal no damage and have no effect."},{"title":"◯ Acidic Body","description":"Anyone who attacks or receives an attack from a Blob will have their weapon or armor dissolve into nothing after 24 hours. This can be avoided by washing the affected weapon or armor with alcohol or wine within that 24 hours."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Jelly-like Material (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 11","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Mini-Blob (1,500G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Blob","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"NQyi7ai5Ut6ytBNZ","name":"Homunculus","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:homunculus","level":5,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Trade Common, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR I p. 422","description":"This is an artificial Human that is believed to have been created during the Ancient Magic Civilization period. Although they are completely Human- like in appearance, they are always expressionless and do not change their facial expressions.\n\nHomunculi were a major source of inspiration for the creation of Runefolk.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":39,"max":39},"mp":{"value":37,"max":37}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 3 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Metamagic/Targets ] and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Jelly-like Material (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 12","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Ancient Writings (2,000G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Homunculus","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Oug9HMdvK3bpczYB","name":"Door Imitator","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:door-limiter","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"-/5 (Floating)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 421","description":"This is a Construct disguised as a door in the corridors of labyrinths, ruins, and discarded mansions. Generally, they are responsible for repelling intruders, remaining completely motionless until an enemy approaches, at which point they attack as soon as they get close enough to open the door.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":22,"max":22},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry/11/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It mimics a door. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If the character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 11, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster can be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"◯ Throw","description":"If the melee attack hits, the target is knocked to the ground and falls prone."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 11","loot":"Magical Wood (200G/Gold Green A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Premium Magical Wood (500G/Gold Green A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Door Imitator","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Qz0kV83LbGhxu6H8","name":"Gattagoil","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gattagoil","level":4,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning-type Damage +3","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 131","description":"This is a type of Gargoyle that resembles a Daemon Nuzumal .\n\nThese creatures often mimic fountain spouts and gutter openings, continuously spewing water from their horizontally split mouths. While commonly found in ruins throughout the Ursyla region, they are rare elsewhere, suggesting they were a regional trend. The Haroon Magical Research Kingdom uses this legend as inspiration for souvenir miniatures. Among these, pieces made using fragments from these monsters themselves or other Gargoyles command high prices.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":35,"max":35},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"Mimics a stone statue. While in the Mimicry state, Monster Knowledge checks cannot be performed against this monster. When approaching carelessly, perform a Danger Sense check with Target Number 12; if failed, you are ambushed. Mimicry automatically ends when taking an action. Mimicry reacts to magic like [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"►Venom Spray / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Sprays venom in &quot;Range: Caster&quot; with &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5.&quot; Targets take 2d points of Poison magic damage.\nThis effect cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Sharp Stone (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"6+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gattagoil","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"RMp69vvtVH4SuqFu","name":"Mono Pawn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mono-pawn","level":2,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallow","reputation":6,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"AB, p. 102","description":"This is a human-sized stone statue with a simple soldier design. They are usually placed in groups and excel at techniques where multiple statues work together to break the enemy's stance and attack.\n\nThe game piece-like design is said to be because they were used in games played during the Magic Civilization Period, but the rules have been lost and are now the subject of scholarly research.\n\nWhile these are mainly found in ruins from the Magic Civilization Period, there are also quite a few examples in the Shallow Abyss. Within the Shallow, they seem to have developed slight variations in their properties, reflecting the desires of skilled players who wanted more challenging rules.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"&#32;","defense":3,"hp":{"value":1,"max":1},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flip Over","description":"When another Mono Pawn exists in the same position (area, coordinate), if a melee attack hits, it knocks prone that target. If the target is a character with multiple sections, this effect requires a number of other Mono Pawns equal to or greater than the number of sections to be present in that position besides itself."},{"title":"◯Hard Mode","description":"This monster receives +2 Defense points while in the Shallow Abyss. Additionally, its weak point changes to &quot;Physical damage +2 points.&quot;"},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Constructs HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mono Pawn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"RweRCEDK5XxTNChB","name":"Thing","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:thing","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"12 (Flow)/-","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"BM","description":"It is a deep blue, jelly-like, amorphous creature, a subspecies of Blob , and is virtually indistinguishable from a regular Blob in appearance. This creature has the ability to mimic creatures and engulf the unwary approaching creatures. The unfortunate prey will be eventually assimilated into a part of the Thing.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":51,"max":51},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Soft Body","description":"Bludgeoning weapons treat the Defense of a Thing as 5 points higher. And it is immune to Throw and similar attacks."},{"title":"◯ Acidic Body","description":"Weapons that have attacked this monster and armor that has been attacked by this monster will melt away after 24 hours; cleaning with alcohol such as wine within 24 hours will prevent this effect."},{"title":"◯ Mimicry / 15 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"It can mimic other living creatures. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with Target Number 15, and if it fails, they will be surprised. Mimicry will automatically end once the monster starts to act."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Jelly-like Material (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Mini Blob (1,500G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Thing","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SzCDyxLgyOKUVvNr","name":"Evil Index","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:evil-index","level":12,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/15 (Floating)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 135","description":"The Evil Index is a Construct known as &quot;The Monster Encyclopedia.&quot; It is a Mimic-type monster that was created by ancient magicians to safeguard their homes and research findings. It appears as a thick book floating in the air, with sharp fangs lining the edges of its binding. When attacking its prey, the book opens slightly, and a shrill laugh can be heard coming from between the fangs. Inside the book, there is a collection of magical knowledge that Evil Index utilizes to launch its attacks.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":103,"max":103},"mp":{"value":96,"max":96}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry / 22 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"It mimics a book. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with Target Number 22, and if it fails, they will be surprised. Mimicry will automatically end once the monster starts to act."},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 10 Level / Magic Power 15 (22)","description":"If you have introduced Deep Magic , it can also cast Deep Magic at the same level and Magic Power."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Golden Bookmark (1,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Spellbook (500G/White A)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Esoteric Spellbook (1,500G/White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Sophisticated Research Data (4,000G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Evil Index","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WxnIJ8wAzwY5UETr","name":"Goldface","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:goldface","level":16,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":22,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"-/15(Floating)","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"20 (27)","source":"CR III p. 381","description":"This is a construct in the shape of a human head from the neck up. It is gigantic, 3 meters in height, and is floating with the help of magic. It is made of a special metal, and its surface is golden and shiny. It has a few curved surfaces, and many small planes are connected by sharp corners and edges to form the face.\n\nDuring the Magic Civilization Period, they were mainly used as gatekeepers of important facilities such as treasuries. Even today, when encountered inside the ruins, the gatekeepers protect such places and act to keep intruders out.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"22 (29)","damage":"2d+20","evasion":"21 (28)","defense":19,"hp":{"value":150,"max":150},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity, ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Superalloy Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from magical or weapon attacks."},{"title":"◯ 3 Actions (At Random)","description":"The monster can take 3 Major Actions in one round. Each Major Action is randomly selected by the table with 1d rolled. The same Major Action may be selected more than once.\n1d | Major Action to be taken |\n1 | ► Face Flash |\n2 | ► Binocular Light Ray |\n3 | ► Gale Blow |\n4 | ► Poisonous Flame Breath |\n5 | ► Crunch |\n6 | Slam (Melee Attack) |"},{"title":"► Face Flash/Can't","description":"Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; causes the target's face to glow intensely, blinding &quot;Target: 2-3 areas (10m Radius) / All&quot;. Targets take a -2 penalty on Accuracy and Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). If the target is hit by this effect again during the duration, the penalty is increased to -4, and the target is blinded (see CR II, p. 70). 3 or more times will not make the effect worse. This effect is curse type and is independent of the target's perception. Target will be affected even if they are blind. If an attempt is made to cancel an effect, the success value is treated as 30."},{"title":"► Binocular Light Ray/20 (27)/Willpower/ Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Line &quot;, light rays are emitted from both eyes, dealing 2d+16 magic damage to the target. For this effect, the dice must be rolled twice to determine at random by 1d whether or not a character in the area of effect has escaped the effect. Only if both of them are the same will the effect be avoided. If either one of the two rolls is a roll that is considered to be affected, then the effect must be taken. Even if both of the rolls are considered to be affected, the effect is taken only once."},{"title":"► Gale Blow/20 (27)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; blowing strong wind from its nose causes &quot;Target: All Areas (30m Radius)/All&quot; to fall prone and take 2d+16 physical damage."},{"title":"► Poisonous Flame Breath/20 (27)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Spits out poisoned particles of high temperature within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Shot &quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20&quot;, dealing 2d+20 Poison and Fire magic damage."},{"title":"► Crunch/21 (28)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Within &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; the monster captures &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with its large mouth and crushes it with its fangs. The target takes 2d+30 points of physical damage. In addition, the target's armor is damaged.\nIf the target is a character that has PC data, the Defense of any equipped armor or shield chosen by the target must be reduced by -1. This effect is cumulative, and if Defense becomes 0, it will be completely destroyed. Armor with reduced Defense can be repaired by paying 10% (up to 90%) of the armor's price for each reduction.\nEach time a character with the monster data is affected by this effect, its Defense is reduced by -1. The effect is cumulative but only down to 0. Defense is restored by +1 point per day."},{"title":"◯ Throw","description":"If a Slam hits the target, the target is knocked prone and falls to the ground."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magical Gold Nuggets (2,000G/Gold Black S)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Pure Mithril (8,800G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Goldface","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WzVRQVOBfIqcMTMe","name":"Caltrop Carpet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:caltrop-carpet","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Labyrinths","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Slashing-type Damage +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"10 (Rotation)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 131","description":"Known as a &quot;trap-type Construct,&quot; while it rarely actively attacks, it lies in wait for those who approach in ruins' corridors, rooms, and in front of doors and treasure chests. These are encountered particularly frequently in the ruins of the Ursyla region, and it is believed that the wizard-king who once ruled this land was their inventor.\n\nIt appears as a cluster of uneven stones spread in a circular pattern on the floor, about 5 meters in diameter. Each stone has been sharply polished and has an irregular shape with multiple protrusions.\n\nWhen approached, several stones leap up to attack. While trying to avoid these, one might step on other stones, unknowingly sustaining serious injuries. The irregular, pointed stones obtained after defeating it are highly valued as materials for folk crafts.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam (Flock)","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":20,"max":20},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Slam (Flock)","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":20,"max":20},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Slam (Flock)","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":20,"max":20},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity, ◯ Slashing Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Swarm","description":"Cannot receive critical hits from any weapon attacks. It cannot be targeted by &quot;Throw&quot; or similar attack methods. Applied damage received from magic that is both &quot;Area: Target&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; is capped at 1 point.\nWhen this monster is in a skirmish state, Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Magic Control ] lose their effects when targeting or including as targets any characters or skirmish areas (center point in Standard/Advanced Combat) within the skirmish area where it exists."},{"title":"◯ Piercing Feet","description":"Characters who end their turn in a skirmish area containing this monster receive fixed damage equal to the number of sections of this monster that have 1 or more HP at that time. Characters that are not grounded, as well as any other Caltrops Carpet in the skirmish, do not receive this effect."},{"title":"►Spread and Mix","description":"To use this effect, the Flock section’s current HP must be 6 points or higher, and it must spend 5 points from it.\nChoose one other Flock section that has 0 or less HP, and revive it with 5 HP. The revived Flock section can act immediately.\nThis effect cannot be used when there are no other Flock sections with 0 or less HP."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"The number of loot Sharp Crystals is reduced by the number of times this monster received Bludgeoning type damage during combat (minimum 0)."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Sharp Crystal (60G/Black B) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Sharp Stone (20G/Black B) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Caltrop Carpet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"XHxmZ1PG7kWfckzr","name":"Familiars I","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:familiars-i","level":0,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Shared with Caster","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":8,"weakness":0,"weakPoint":"None","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"5 (4 Legs)/10 (Swimming)","fortitude":"-","willpower":"-","source":"CR I p. 434","description":"This is data for Familiars that can be summoned with the Truespeech Magic spell [ Familiar ].\n\nSee also: Common Abilities of Familiars .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tongue","accuracy":"1 (8)","damage":"2d-2","evasion":"1 (8)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Frog's Body","description":"The frog can move underwater. Its mobility is equal to that of a normal frog."},{"title":"Spider","description":"Initiative: 11\nMovement Speed: 7 (Many Legs)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nBite | 1 (8) | 2d-2 | | 2 (9) | 0 | | - | 7 |"},{"title":"◯Spider's Body","description":"The spider can move freely on walls and ceilings. While sticking to the ceiling, it will not be targeted by a wide range of effects unless the enemy specifically targets the Familiar. Its mobility is equal to a recluse spider."},{"title":"Bird","description":"Initiative: 13\nMovement Speed: -/30 (Flying)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nBeak | 2 (9) | 2d-1 | | 2 (9) | 0 | | - | 7 |"},{"title":"◯Bird's Body","description":"Capable of flight. Physical ability is that of a normal bird."},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Bird Familiar receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"Cat","description":"Initiative: 12\nMovement Speed: 12 (4 Legs)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nClaws | 3 (10) | 2d | | 3 (10) | 1 | | - | 7 |"},{"title":"◯Cat's Body","description":"Can pass through narrow gaps, etc. Physical ability is the same as an ordinary housecat."},{"title":"◯Gives Darkvision","description":"Shares its Darkvision with its Master."},{"title":"Snake","description":"Initiative: 12\nMovement Speed: 10 (Slithering)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nBite | 2 (9) | 2d-1 | | 2 (9) | 1 | | - | 7 |"},{"title":"◯Snake's Body","description":"The snake can pass through extremely narrow spaces. Its physical ability is equal to that of the normal snake."},{"title":"◯Toxic Tooth","description":"When a Snake Familiar makes a melee attack and hits, it automatically deals 1 Poison magic damage to the target of the melee attack. This ability only works if the Familiar is in Touch range with the Master.\n<div"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Familiars I","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":100000}
{"_id":"Y0ozTVKfxxBtkcwK","name":"Familiar from Beyond","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:familiar-from-beyond","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Shared with Caster","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Daemonic, Arcana","habitat":"Various, Shallows","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"14 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"-","willpower":"-","source":"AB, p. 102","description":"This is a familiar that can be commanded by Daemons who use Truespeech Magic at level 4 or higher. It has an appearance similar to an Aetherbeast . Created using the Daemon's own blood as a medium, it possesses base abilities that surpass ordinary Familiars and gains the ability to act independently like a Familiar II. It can turn invisible and is often used for reconnaissance.\n\nDue to its creation method, only Daemons can create it, but it leaves behind &quot;Daemon's Blood&quot; as loot. In times of crisis for its master, it may sacrifice itself in a self-destruction attack. Though its Daemon master likely won't feel any sentiment toward such desperate loyalty.\n\nUnlike regular familiars, it doesn't possess the [◯One Mind, One Character] ability (see CR I, p. 433, ML. p. 235) and has its own independent HP. It also lacks [◯Fall Resistance] and takes normal falling damage.\n\nWithin a Shallow Abyss, it has the [Shared Visibility] power possessed by Familiars II, increasing its master's threat level.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"&#32;","defense":4,"hp":{"value":3,"max":3},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Daemon Familiar","description":"The following abilities are common to these familiars. For individual details, see CR I, p. 432, or ML, p. 235.\n[◯Poison Immunity], [◯Disease Immunity], [◯Psychic Immunity], [◯Can be Detected], [◯Familiar Contract], [◯Familiars Knowledge = Sorcerers], [◯Shared MP], [◯Resistance Sharing], [◯Senses Sharing]"},{"title":"◯Free Will","description":"Unlike regular Familiars ([◯Will-less]), Familiars from Beyond possess their own will. They are capable of communication using Arcana and Daemonic languages. However, they maintain unwavering loyalty to their master and will never take actions that would constitute betrayal."},{"title":"◯Shared Visibility (Shallow)","description":"This effect only applies when both the master and this monster are within the same Shallow Abyss.\nThe caster can use this monster's line of sight to cast spells. However, the point of origin for spell casting is always the caster. When considering range distance, it must be calculated from the caster's position, and spells with &quot;Area: Shot &quot; or &quot;Area: Line &quot; are fired from the caster.\nWhen casting spells from the familiar's viewpoint as a Major Action, both the master and this monster complete their Major Actions. When cast as a Minor Action, both are considered to have performed Minor Actions."},{"title":"►Invisibility","description":"This effect requires 5 MP points to use.\nAgainst characters with &quot;Perception: Five Senses&quot; or &quot;Perception: Mechanical&quot;, it becomes invisible (see CR II, p. 69). Characters with &quot;Perception: Magic&quot; can still detect its presence.\nInvisibility is maintained unless it performs a Full Move or Major Action, in which case it automatically ends immediately after."},{"title":"►Desperate Self-Destruct / Can't","description":"This effect can only be used when its current HP is at or below one-fourth (rounded up) of its maximum HP.\nMakes a special attack against &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; with &quot;Range/Area: 2(20m) / Shot &quot; and self-destructs. Deals &quot;2d+6&quot; points of Fire magic damage to the target. When using this effect, the Familiar from Beyond's HP automatically becomes &quot;0&quot; and it is destroyed."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Daemon's Blood (100G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Familiar from Beyond","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Y7sz1PEkmeOl1pPY","name":"Buckbaird","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:buckbaird","level":12,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/14 (Flying)","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR II p. 383","description":"A giant monster about 1m in diameter, a Buckbaird has one giant eye in the front and many much smaller eyes around its body. It's covered in fine black fur and floats using a mysterious power. The front eye has incredible magical power and can fire five different rays at targets in front of it. Due to the structure of the eye, only one ray can be used at a time. In combat, the Buckbaird combines the usage of these rays with incredibly fast tackling attacks, making it dangerous both in melee and at a range.\n\nThere are many mysteries about the ecology of the Buckbaird, and it is thought that they are the creation of some mad wizard during the Magic Civilization period. However, their origin and diet are unknown, and even their thoughts and possible breeding habits are an absolute mystery. What little is known is they enjoy the spaces in underground labyrinths.\n\nAlthough it can speak Arcana for guidance, it is unable to communicate and speaks a stream of unintelligible gibberish one-sidedly.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":117,"max":117},"mp":{"value":90,"max":90}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Triple Attack &amp; Inconsistent","description":"Buckbaird can take three Major Actions in one round. They are chosen randomly from among Slams and five types of eye rays."},{"title":"► Eye Ray/15 (22)/Willpower/Negates","description":"With &quot;Range: 20m&quot; and &quot;Area: Shot ,&quot; a ray of light is shot from the magic eye at one enemy character. Buckbaird has five types of rays. A character cannot be targeted by more than one Eye Ray but can be targeted by Slams and one Eye Ray.\n1: Paralyzing Ray\nThe target reduces their Dexterity and Agility by 12 points (to a minimum of 0) for 30 seconds (3 rounds). For fixed value characters, each paralyzing ray adds a -2 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks, respectively. This effect is cumulative.\n2: Sleep Ray\nThe target falls into a deep sleep for 3 hours. This effect is Psychic type. Target cannot be woken up by normal means. This effect can be dispelled via magic means by contested check.\n3: Frost Ray\nFrost Ray deals 2d+20 Water/Ice damage to the target.\n4: Brainwashing Ray\nThose affected will follow the Buckbaird's orders and move to protect it for the next one minute (6 rounds). Orders given cannot be harmful to the target. Without a specific command, the target will act to protect the Buckbaird. This effect is Psychic type.\n5: Rust Ray\nThose affected lose all metal objects of A-Rank or lower, including weapons, armor, shields, and accessories.\nS-Rank metal objects, as well as those from the Magic Civilization and earlier, remain unaffected."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Buckbaird receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Giant Eyeball (500G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Crystallized Magical Eye (1,000G/Gold Red S)"},{"roll":"9 - 12","loot":"Crystallized Magical Eyes (1,000G/Gold Red S) x 1d"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Crystallized Magical Eyes (1,000G/Gold Red S) x 2d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Buckbaird","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YTBnGvskCZh2XcM8","name":"Unruly Sand Ghast","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:unruly-sand-ghast","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Deserts","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Floating)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 127","description":"Originally a group of about ten Sand Ghasts , their Regenerative Nuclei became so closely packed together that they went out of control with their magical power and merged to form a single Construct. The body of the Construct is composed of desert sand.\n\nThe Construct is centered around a floating sphere with a diameter of about 3 meters. Several tentacles, each several meters long, protrude from the center of the sphere. Near the tip of each tentacle, the shape of a human body is retained, typical of a Sand Ghast.\n\nSimilar to the common Sand Ghast, this creature is dangerous and will attack anything. The &quot;Agglomerated Regenerative Nucleus&quot; obtained from this monster is traded as a material for &quot;Sand Armor II&quot; (see Natural History of Burlight p. 42).","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Body)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}},{"style":"Strike (Tentacle)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}},{"style":"Strike (Tentacle)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}},{"style":"Strike (Tentacle)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}},{"style":"Strike (Tentacle)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}},{"style":"Strike (Tentacle)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Sand Body","description":"It does not receive a critical hit from any attack that deals physical damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯Core Regeneration = 7 points","description":"At the end of its turn, all sections regain 7 points of HP. This ability has no effect on sections with 0 or less HP. This ability is lost for all sections if the HP of the Body section receives magic damage which is dealt with a critical hit."},{"title":"⏩Tentacle Revival","description":"The Body resurrects and restores a Tentacle section whose HP is 0 or less to 20 points of HP. When this effect is used, the current negative HP of the Tentacle section just before the revival plus 10 points are consumed from the Body section (e.g., if a Tentacle section with -3 points of HP is revived, 13 points will be consumed).\nThe revived Tentacle section cannot act immediately after its revival. It can act from the next turn of this monster."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"The Loot item &quot;Agglomerated Regenerative Nucleus&quot; is not gained if the Body section receives additional magical damage caused by a critical hit during combat."},{"title":"Tentacle","description":""},{"title":"🗨Decoy Attack I","description":"Knows the [ Decoy Attack I ] Combat Feat."},{"title":"🗨△Cover I (Body only)","description":"Knows the [ Cover I ] Combat Feat. Only the Body section can be targeted with this feat."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Agglomerated Regenerative Nucleus (2,500G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Dense Magic Jewel (700G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Unruly Sand Ghast","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Ybk54s8nk1Zl4T0q","name":"Plasma Sphere","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:plasma-sphere","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/10(Floating)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR III p. 375","description":"This construct looks like a about 30cm in diameter crystal ball floating in the space. Lightning is swirling inside the sphere and occasionally discharges outward with sound.\n\nIts lightning can activate Constructs and Magitech. It is known that this Construct was developed by researchers in the Magic Civilization Period, but it was later confirmed to be effective for Magitech as well. In the Magitech Civilization Period, there were cases where Magitech was used at archaeological sites.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Shock","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":53,"max":53},"mp":{"value":34,"max":34}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Shock","description":"Melee Attack damage inflicted by this monster is treated as Lightning magic damage."},{"title":"► Lightning Connection/Can't","description":"Deals &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; at &quot;Range: Touch&quot; 5 Lightning fixed damage.\nIf the target is a Construct or Magitech monster, the target gets a +2 bonus to Accuracy check for 10 seconds (1 round), and the physical damage it causes becomes Lightning type and increased by +3 points."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Lightning Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Plasma Sphere","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ZK64MapnQp5yJfQE","name":"Ghast Bishop","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast-bishop","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR III p. 375","description":"It is a Ghast that has grown to an immensely powerful level, often leading an army of Ghasts and playing the role of Ghast leader.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arms","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":54,"max":54},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Dense Magic Jewel (700G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast Bishop","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ckQ8VE6LKAze1ceP","name":"Malicious Dresser","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:malicious-dresser","level":8,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR III p. 382","description":"This is a runaway construct of a magical mirror stand used by the nobility in the Magic Civilization Period. It is equipped with three large mirrors reflecting the whole body and is supported by a sturdy base.\n\nIts original purpose was to place the reflected image outside the mirror in order to be able to check it from all angles, but what is now running amok in ruins is to take the reflected character into the mirror and manipulate only its shadow.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Mirror)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":61,"max":61},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}},{"style":"None (Mirror)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":61,"max":61},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}},{"style":"None (Mirror)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":61,"max":61},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}},{"style":"Kick (Foundation)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":69,"max":69},"mp":{"value":15,"max":15}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Mirror","description":""},{"title":"► Invitation to the Reversed World/10 (17)/ Willpower/Negates","description":"Engulfs the person reflected in the mirror, making it impossible to interfere with the real world.\nEngulfs &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; in the mirror within &quot;Range: Touch.&quot; The captured target will not be able to perform any movement or actions (Major Action, Minor Action). The target can attempt to escape at the beginning of its turn by comparing the success value of the ability to its Willpower (with the escaping player being the active player). If the success value is higher than the ability value, the target is released and can continue its turn. Otherwise, the target suffers 2d+5 Curse magic damage.\nThis effect is automatically canceled when the HP of the Mirror section that used this ability becomes 0 or less or the target dies.\nA Mirror section that already captured another character cannot use this ability.\nAs a general rule, this ability does not allow a character in multiple sections to be the target. However, suppose multiple Mirror sections have not engulfed the character. In that case, using this ability, it is possible to take in as many sections of the target by the same number of Mirror sections. Each check of this ability and each check of escape attempts is performed only once to compare to the success value. Damage incurred in case of escape failure is given to each section individually."},{"title":"► Mirroring","description":"This ability can only be used if another character has been taken in by [ ► Invitation to the Reversed World].\nThe mirror creates the shadow of the character captured in the mirror and manipulated at will. The abilities and numerical values of the character captured in the mirror are used as they are. The GM controls the shadow.\nWhen a shadow performs an action involving an item's consumption, it does so by consuming that item from the character captured in the mirror (but it does not needlessly discard items, etc.).\nThe shadow itself has no HP or MP, and if it must be dealt damage or consumed, the HP and MP of the Mirror section controlling it are reduced instead.\nWhen Mirror's turn is over, the shadow disappears.\nOnly one Mirror section can perform the [ ► Mirroring] per turn. Once one Mirror section has done so, no other section Mirror can use it.\nWhen multiple Mirror section is used to capture the character with multiple sections, it is possible to create the shadow of only one of the sections."},{"title":"Foundation","description":""},{"title":"◯ Oak Wood Body","description":"It is immune to a critical hit from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Size prevents enemies from attacking it.\nAll Mirror sections receive a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect disappears when the Foundation section falls to 0 HP or lower."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Fragments of Mirror (330G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Large Fragments of Mirror (1,220G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Malicious Dresser","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"cl0RHDGOIYFeYTzt","name":"Cheap Stone","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cheap-stone","level":2,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Caves, Ruins","reputation":7,"weakness":10,"weakPoint":"Energy type damage +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"8 (Rotation)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 420","description":"These are palm-sized rocks found at Magic Civilization Period sites, etc. They are monsters that were moved out of the ground during the mining of mako stone, etc. They were called scrap stones or cheap stones and were considered of little or no value.\n\nWhen a creature with mana approaches, it may start to move. It does not fly but only rolls and scoots along the ground.\n\nThey have no purpose for their behavior but move around and sometimes bump into each other. However, they are sometimes found clustered together in piles of soil, and there have been sightings of them gathering at the feet of people in ruins.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d+1","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":13,"max":13},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Crawl In/2 (9)/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It moves under the feet of &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range: Touch&quot; and causes the target to fall prone."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10 - 11","loot":"Mako Stone (1 pts.) (50G)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Mako Stone (2 pts.) (100G)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cheap Stone","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"clMwbslU7k6pwUXO","name":"Carbide Claws","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:carbide-claws","level":14,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":19,"weakness":25,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"17","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"CR III p. 380","description":"It is a bipedal golem made of a jet-black alloy, but with long arms that reach to the ground and huge hands.\n\nAs the guardian of places and treasures, it is known to throw anything that approaches and never allows it to pass.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist (Right Side)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+21","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":20,"hp":{"value":120,"max":120},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Fist (Left Side)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+21","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":20,"hp":{"value":120,"max":120},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Knowledge = Conjurer Class","description":"Those with Conjurer will automatically succeed in the Monster Knowledge check for this monster. But they still must roll to know its weak point."},{"title":"◯ Superalloy Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from magical or weapon attacks."},{"title":"► Throw/17 (24)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The Carbide Claws attempts to grab a &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range: Touch.&quot; If successful, the target is thrown to the rearguard area of their faction (Simplified Combat) or in any direction chosen by this monster at 30m (Standard Combat) and falls down, taking 45 points of fall damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magic Iron Ingot (680G/Gold Black A) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Pure Mithril (8,800G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Carbide Claws","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dN2rAAlDyEGesFiE","name":"Disaster Tome","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:disaster-tome","level":11,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"High","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/15(Flying)","fortitude":"13(20)","willpower":"15(22)","source":"AB, p. 107","description":"Disaster Tome appears as a thick book with its locks popped open with detailed records of every disaster that has occurred in this world. The records are not just text - it is a powerful Construct that can recreate the scenes and circumstances of those times.\n\nThough it was originally created for record-keeping, in its pursuit of gathering more records, it has become an entity that causes disasters itself. While it's possible to communicate with it using arcana, it's obsessed with causing and recording disasters, making productive negotiation hopeless.\n\nStrangely, there are records of disasters that shouldn't have been recorded in the past, leading to speculation that these are premonitions of future disasters.\n\nWhile this monster is typically seen in ruins, there have been cases where it was spotted in the Shallow Abyss. In such cases, this monster becomes more persistent in recreating disasters.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"13(20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":13,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight II","description":"Gains a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Capricious","description":"This monster's actions are randomly chosen between Slam (melee attack) and 5 types of [►Disaster Recreation]. Roll 1d each turn to determine the action. If [►Disaster Recreation] is selected but the required MP cannot be consumed, the action changes to Slam.\n1d | Action |\n1 | ►Disaster Recreation: Meteor Shower |\n2 | ►Disaster Recreation: Tsunami |\n3 | ►Disaster Recreation: Pandemic |\n4 | ►Disaster Recreation: Fire Tornado |\n5 | ►Disaster Recreation: Social Unrest |\n6 | Slam |"},{"title":"►Disaster Recreation: Meteor Shower / 15 (22) / Willpower / Half","description":"This effect consumes 30 MP points.\nA rain of meteors pours down.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster&quot; it deals &quot;2d+30&quot; points of bludgeoning magic damage to &quot;Target: All Areas (50m radius) / All.&quot;"},{"title":"►Disaster Recreation: Tsunami / 15 (22) / Fortitude / Half","description":"This effect consumes 20 MP points.\nA tsunami sweeps through.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: All areas (20m radius) / All&quot;, it deals &quot;2d+22&quot; points of Water/Ice magic damage.\nAdditionally, targets that fail their resistance check are pushed back 20m and knocked prone. In Simplified combat, they are forcibly moved to the rearguard area of their faction. In Standard/Advanced Combat, they are moved to a position 20m away from this monster along the line connecting the monster and the target. If they were at the same coordinates as this monster, they are moved 20m in any direction of the monster's choosing."},{"title":"►Disaster Recreation: Pandemic / 15 (22) / Fortitude / Half","description":"This effect consumes 20 MP points.\nA severe infection occurs.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: All areas (20m radius)/All&quot;, it deals &quot;2d+20&quot; points of Disease magic damage.\nWhen multiple characters are simultaneously targeted by this effect, they perform resistance checks one character at a time in order of proximity to this monster (if characters are in the same position, the GM determines the order). If there is a failure, the Target Number for this resistance check increases by +1. This effect is cumulative."},{"title":"►Disaster Recreation: Fire Tornado / 15 (22) / Willpower / Half","description":"This effect consumes 15 MP points.\nA spiral of fire rushes through.\nIt deals &quot;2d+20&quot; points of Fire and Wind magic damage within &quot;Range/area: 2 (50m) / Line .&quot;"},{"title":"►Disaster Recreation: Social Unrest / 15 (22) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This effect consumes 15 MP points.\nA wave of distrust and discord dominates everything.\nWithin &quot;Range: Caster&quot;, applies an effect to &quot;Target: All Areas (50m radius) / All.&quot; Targets that fail the resistance power check will reject all effects with &quot;Resistance: Optional&quot; that are placed on them. Additionally, they cannot use any friendly effects (such as those that heal HP or add skill check bonuses) on others.\nThis effect is Psychic type and lasts for 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"◯MP Regeneration = 5 points (Shallow)","description":"At the end of its turn, recovers 5 MP. This effect only appears when this monster is inside the Shallow Abyss."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Golden Bookmark (1,000G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 12","loot":"Fragment of Disaster (900G/White A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Fragment of Unknown Disaster (3,600G/White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Disaster Tome","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dcDPkhT0EQUnKcmM","name":"Phosphor Sphere","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:phosphor-sphere","level":9,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Underground Labyrinths, Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/16(Flying)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR III p. 377","description":"It is a sphere about one meter in diameter that floats while emitting phosphorescent light. This construct is believed to have been used by wizards to show off their creations and illuminate them.\n\nAs well as being a light, it could act as a guardian, preventing the exhibits from being stolen or damaged.\n\nIt is often encountered in ruins, along with the architecture and objects it was guarding. Although it does not speak itself, there have been reports of it being stopped by Arcana language words.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":74,"max":74},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity, ◯ Lightning Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Energy Absorption","description":"It is immune to Energy-type damage. Conversely, if the monster is hit by an Energy-type attack, its HP is recovered by the amount of applied damage.\nNo effects other than damage can be caused by Energy-type effects."},{"title":"◯ Poison/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Slam hits, it deals 2d Poison magic damage to the target."},{"title":"◯ Poison Body/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"A character who makes a melee attack against this monster and hits it suffers 2d points of Poison magic damage at the end of their turn."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Green Dye (80G/Green B) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Green Light Powder (520G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Green Light Powder (520G/Gold A) x 1d"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Phosphor Sphere","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"g1lZNQ9Id6LSjw8p","name":"Ghast Knight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast-knight","level":4,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":7,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"8","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 422","description":"These Ghast Knights have been trained to use weapons and still retain some martial prowess from when they were once alive. Now able to fight and move efficiently, their understanding of commands has grown as well. They can be seen commanding other weaker Ghasts .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":32,"max":32},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 11","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Dense Magic Jewel (700G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast Knight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gQ0PKH9rhJJshnPi","name":"Ghast King","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast-king","level":13,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":16,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"10/-","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 135","description":"It is called the Ghast King and is the control point of all Ghasts . It looks like a giant Ghast without hands, and has no offensive abilities of its own. However, it can summon an inexhaustible number of Ghast species with its never-ending magic power, and can strengthen them. It can also make Ghasts disappear and create a storm with its mana, making it difficult for even moderately skilled adventurers to deal with it.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":127,"max":127},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ 3 Actions","description":"It can take 3 Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Ghast Enhancing","description":"The Ghast King enhances all Ghasts , including itself, within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; with &quot;Target: All Areas (20m Radius) / All.&quot; Targets gain a +1 bonus to all Skill Checks and +2 points to Damage and Defense for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative."},{"title":"► Ghast Summoning","description":"Ghast King summons a Ghast within &quot;Range: Touch.&quot; The Ghast to be summoned is selected from 1 x Ghast Queen , 2 x Ghast Bishop , 3 x Ghast Knight , or 6 x Ghast Lurker . On the same round it cannot summon the same types of Ghasts (but can summon the same Ghasts on different rounds). Summoned Ghasts can start their actions immediately.\nThis ability cannot be used on the turn when [ ► Ghast Rampage] is used."},{"title":"► Ghast Rampage / Can't","description":"The monster causes the magic power of the Ghast it follows to go out of control, creating a storm of mana. This unique skill is effective for “ Target: 1 area (5m radius) / Space&quot; with &quot;Range: Caster&quot;. Up to 5 Ghasts within the area of this unique skill die and inflict physical damage of (2d x the number of Ghast species destroyed) points to all selected characters within the area.\nThis ability can be used only once per round. Also, a Ghast King cannot use this ability on the turn it used [ ► Ghast Summoning]."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Glittering Magic Stone (1,200G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast King","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gnqvko30LlHQzoW6","name":"Purple Blob","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:purple-blob","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Marshes, Ruins, Shallows","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"6 (Crawling)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"AB, p. 105","description":"A Purple Blob is a translucent, jelly-like monster. Blobs are Constructs created during Magic Civilization Period experiments; this is a variety that has gone feral in a Shallow Abyss. The purple liquid that makes up its body is both a strong acid and has been altered by the Shallow's shadow influence, inflicting the curse of the Abyss on any target it touches.\n\nWhether it escaped from a crumbling Shallow or not, it is occasionally discovered outside the Shallow. Though it cannot spread a Shallow's curses, it remains a dangerous entity that engulfs and dissolves anything that carelessly approaches it.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":7,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Soft Body","description":"When receiving damage from blunt weapons, treat Defense as 5 points higher. The Blob cannot be targeted by Throws or similar attack methods."},{"title":"◯Engulf / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"When a Slam attack hits, the target is engulfed inside the body. The target cannot move or take any Major Actions, and at the end of this monster's turn, must take 2d+5 points of magic damage.\nThe engulfed target can attempt a Fortitude check once during their turn to escape if successful. Once this check is made, their turn immediately ends regardless of the result."},{"title":"◯Abyssal Acidic Body","description":"This effect only occurs within a Shallow Abyss.\nWeapons that hit this monster, or armor worn when hit by this monster, immediately receive one random Abyss Enhancement (see AB p. 38) and one Abyss Curse (see AB p. 40). This effect does not stack, and both enhancements and curses will disappear if cleaned with wine or other alcohol within 24 hours.\nIf 24 hours pass while under this effect, an additional Abyss Curse is added, and all enhancements and curses become permanent. The two Abyss Curses gained from this effect cannot have their contents redetermined (see AB p. 41)."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Abyssal Acid (300G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Strong Abyssal Acid (900G/Gold Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Purple Blob","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kst6tm8NdokSHOrj","name":"Shadow Teamster","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shadow-teamster","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"VC","description":"This Construct is black and about 1.5 meters long. Its upper body is Humanoid, and it has several long, thin, cloth-like legs. It waits in the shadow of its master when not in use, and only performs chores when called. In the present day, it wanders around the ruins as it cannot find its master's shadow.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon (Body)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":44,"max":44},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Kick (Legs)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":29,"max":29},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attitude Control","description":"It can never fall prone due to any effect."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Regrow Legs","description":"If the Legs section HP is 0 or less, it is restored to its maximum value. The recovered Legs section can perform an action immediately.\nThis ability can be used only once per combat."},{"title":"Legs","description":""},{"title":"◯ Outstretched Legs","description":"Kick attacks are treated as melee attacks with &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot;."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shadow Teamster","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lLdUOpZK4m7lqUpa","name":"Dungeon Keeper","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dungeon-keeper","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Abandoned Buildings","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10/-","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p.132","description":"This is a cleaning Construct probably made in the Magic Civilization Period. Inside its humanoid body, cleaning tools such as brooms, dustpans, and cloths are stored. Detergent can be sprayed from the base of the two legs and is sprayed on the floor or low places.\n\nThe appearance of many of them reflects the taste and aesthetic sense of their makers, and there is little uniformity in their design, ranging from those that are utilitarian to those that are highly valued as works of art.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Broom","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":24,"max":24},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Attitude Control","description":"It does not fall prone under any effect."},{"title":"► Detergent Spray / Can't","description":"The detergent is sprayed in &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / Space&quot; within &quot;Range: Caster&quot;. All targets within this range, if they are on their feet, must make an Acrobatics check with Target Number of 10 at the beginning of their turn, failing which they will fall prone immediately. If the character falls, they cannot get up during their turn.\nThis effect lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Magical Wood (200G/Red Green A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Premium Magical Wood (500G/Red Green A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dungeon Keeper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lr302YWE3txpYZL3","name":"Scarlet Stamp","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:scarlet-stamp","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15 (Leaping)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 379","description":"This Construct was created in the Magic Civilization Period and has a caterpillar-like body with a sucker-like mouth. It was mainly used for guarding and eliminating intruders. It moves with its body wriggling and jumping and attacks hostile objects by sucking on them with its sucker pads and sucking up their bodily fluids. The name is derived from the bruises left on the target after the suckers were attached.\n\nIt also has the power to suck up mana and cancel all weak magic and effects, and as a byproduct of this effect, it may have crystals with mana stored in its body. They can be used in exactly the same way as the mako stone.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Suction Pad","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":59,"max":59},"mp":{"value":22,"max":22}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Dangerous Absorption/Can't","description":"If an attack with the Suction Pad hits the target, it is sucked into the target. In the sucking state, the monster can use one of the unique skills [ ⏩ Suck Blood] or [ ⏩ Minor Break]. If the turn ends without using any of the unique skills, the monster automatically releases the target."},{"title":"⏩ Suck Blood/Can't","description":"It deals 2d magic damage to the target and heals its own HP by the same amount as the applied damage.\nThis unique skill can only be used on targets that were sucked with [ ◯ Dangerous Absorption] and once used targets are released."},{"title":"⏩ Minor Break/Can't","description":"Removes any effect from the target with a success value of 0.\nThis unique skill can only be used on targets sucked with [ ◯ Dangerous Absorption], and targets are released once used."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"5 - 6","loot":"Mako Stone (1 pts.)(50G)"},{"roll":"7 - 9","loot":"Mako Stone (2 pts.)(100G)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Mako Stone (5 pts.)(250G)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Scarlet Stamp","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"mzfeg4VZuwqCIoBM","name":"Perlas Cloud","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:perlas-cloud","level":9,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Marshes, Ruins, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"-/18(Flying)","fortitude":"12(19)","willpower":"11(18)","source":"AB, p. 106","description":"This is a gaseous-bodied Construct, usually spread thin and difficult to notice. It is said to be a feral variant of guardians created during the Magic Civilization Period.\n\nWhen combat begins, it coalesces into a humanoid form. At this time, its gaseous purple coloration becomes apparent. The gas mass attacks with sufficient hardness and mass, but when weapons are swung at it, it reduces its density to let them pass through harmlessly. To land an effective hit, one must use a weapon imbued with magical power.\n\nIt is frequently sighted in Shallow Abysses. It is believed that the Shallow environment is particularly suitable for maintaining its unstable body, resulting in a notably high survival rate.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arms","accuracy":"12(19)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"&#32;","defense":11,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Normal Weapon Immunity, ◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"◯Gaseous Form","description":"Cannot receive critical hits from attack types other than Fire type and Wind type."},{"title":"◯Fire Vulnerability","description":"When receiving Fire type damage, automatically takes an additional 3 points of damage."},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"Gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Hard to Detect / 18 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"Drifts as a thinly spread gaseous form, waiting for an opportunity. When approaching within 10m of this monster, failing a Danger Sense check with target number 18 results in being surprised.\nInside a Shallow Abyss, detection becomes even more difficult, and the Danger Sense check Target Number becomes 20."},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Perlas Cloud can make two Arms attacks each round, though each attack requires an Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"►Smoke Screen / Can't","description":"This effect can only be used when its current HP is at half or less of its maximum HP (rounded up), and costs 10 MP to use.\nTransform its body into gas and disperse. Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5&quot;, deal 2d+9 points of Poison magic damage. Afterwards, it enters a dispersed state in the surroundings. In this state, it cannot receive any physical damage.\nThe Perlas Cloud returns to humanoid form at the start of its next turn. At this time, it automatically recovers 10 HP. If it is within a Shallow Abyss, the recovery amount is 15 points."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Malignant Gas (400G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Dangerous Gas (2,400G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Perlas Cloud","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"n4WfPLEfokjq9QQi","name":"Creeping Coin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:creeping-coin","level":2,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Flying)","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"BM","description":"This Construct is similar to a small pile of gold coins; about 20 gold coins make up one Creeping Coin. If any of them is unintentionally approached, it will jump up and spit fire. There is no end to the number of new adventurers who are burned to death by what they believed were large gold coins. Rarely, real gold coins are mixed in.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d-1","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":16,"max":16},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry / 12 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"It disguises itself as gold coins. While it is mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with Target Number 12, and if it fails, they will be surprised. Mimicry will automatically end once the monster starts to act."},{"title":"► Flame Breath / 3 (10) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Within “ Range / Area:1 (5m) / Shot ,&quot; spits fire at &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;, dealing &quot;2d+2&quot; Fire-type magic damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Old Gold Coin (100G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Creeping Coin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oV6SsGrm7ZEw4Dxi","name":"Casting Hand","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:casting-hand","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"-/11 (Floating)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"AB, p. 104","description":"This is a Construct in the form of a large floating hand. Its fingers are long and eerie, each adorned with rings, and it constantly appears to be tracing magic characters in the air.\n\nAs a Construct created to be a guardian, it is often found protecting specific locations or serving as an escort for its caster.\n\nIts extremely unsettling appearance is thought to be composed of severed wrist and fingers of the magic users, though this is uncertain. Perhaps due to a shortage of materials, some have been spotted with fewer than five fingers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Play (Fingers (1-5))","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"&#32;","defense":8,"hp":{"value":4,"max":4},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"None (Wrist)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"&#32;","defense":7,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Finger","description":""},{"title":"►Limited Truespeech Magic / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":"Among Truespeech Magic, only the following spells can be cast with Magic Power 6: [ Energy Bolt ], [ Reaping Slash ], [ Lightning ], [ Blast ], and [ Fireball ]."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Hawk Eye ]."},{"title":"◯Isolated Finger","description":"Each Finger section is subject to the following restrictions:\nIt cannot cast magic that another Finger section has already cast in that turn. If another Finger section has already cast magic in that turn, its Magic Power is reduced by 1 for each casting Finger section."},{"title":"🗨Magic Power Concentration","description":"This effect can only be declared when there are other inactive Finger sections that have not yet acted this turn.\nIts Magic Power increases by +1 for each inactive Finger section. When this effect is declared, all other inactive Finger sections complete their Major Action.\nThis effect lasts only 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect cannot be declared if the Wrist section's HP is 0 or below."},{"title":"Wrist","description":""},{"title":"◯Finger Command","description":"Grants the ability [Magic Power Concentration] to Finger section. This effect is lost when Wrist section's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"►Finger Regeneration","description":"This effect can only be used within a Shallow Abyss.\nConsumes 15 HP to restore the current HP of one selected Finger section to 15 points. Regeneration is possible even if the Finger section's HP is already at 0 or below, and the Finger section can utilize all of its abilities. Additionally, it can act from that turn."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Rough Ring (50G/Gold White B)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Silver Ring (250G/Gold White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Yellowed Golden Ring (1,000G/Gold White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Casting Hand","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pe09vYJUWPL029DE","name":"Trap Mixer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:trap-mixer","level":4,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 150","description":"This is a 2-meter-long, insect-like construct that lacks wings for flying. Instead, three to five spinning gears are attached to its back near the top, and it strikes opponents by creating razor winds through the violent rotation of these gears.\n\nAttacking the gears on the wings increases the speed of rotation and produces stronger winds. It is worth noting that this type of aircraft was initially used for autonomous air cages and other non-combat roles.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Feathers","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":38,"max":38},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Rotary Conversion","description":"Whenever the monster receives 1 point or more physical damage, the monster's physical damage and magic damage are increased by 1 point for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is stacks until it reaches a maximum of 4 points."},{"title":"► Whirlwind/5 (12)/Willpower/Half","description":"Trap Mixer creates a magical wind around itself. It deals 2d wind magic damage to all opponents in the same skirmish area.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"► Howling Wind/6 (13)/Willpower/Half","description":"Trap Mixer sends wind blade far. With &quot;Area: Shot &quot; it deals 2d+2 slashing magic damage to target 1 character within &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot;.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Enchanted Oak Branch (200G/Gold Green A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Trap Mixer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qB1DjdH0xi2ueunD","name":"Swordmaton","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:swordmaton","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"(15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR II p. 378","description":"This is a combat training construct from the Magic Civilization Period. It has a log-like body with three arms holding weapons and four short legs for movement. Rarely a working version of this construct has been found at Magic Civilization Period ruins.\n\nIt is said to have been used to teach how to deal with various weapons and magical attacks. Its three arms were modeled after a certain humanoid race that became extinct during the Magic Civilization Period.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Body)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":49,"max":49},"mp":{"value":36,"max":36}},{"style":"Sword (Sword Arm)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":34,"max":34},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Spear (Spear Arm)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":38,"max":38},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Club (Club Arm)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Stable Body","description":"Any &quot;Resistance: Half&quot; effect on this monster will be treated as &quot;Resistance: Negates.&quot;"},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 5 Level /Magic Power 7 (14)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"Sword Arm/Spear Arm/Club Arm","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Decoy Attack I","description":"It gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +2 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -1 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to -4 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Book of Mastership (300G/White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Crude Weapon (10G/Black White B)"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"High-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Engraved Weapon (600G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Swordmaton","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qxeJGy5bBYrMc2eT","name":"Ghost Servant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghost-servant","level":8,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 132","description":"Cyrecode, which belongs to the Haroon Magical Research Kingdom, is a city that concentrates its population on floating rock formations. There, a small number of floating Construct Ghost Curtains in the form of transparent cloth have survived the Magic Civilization Period and continue to float.\n\nGhost Servants are said to have been created as precursors to these Ghost Curtains to establish the abilities of transparency and luminescence.\n\nAlthough transparent, their crude clay doll-like shape appears faintly visible due to the distortion of the surrounding scenery. The sages have concluded that this was caused by the thickness of their bodies, and overcoming this flaw led to the development of the Ghost Curtain.\n\nLike various other Constructs, they were primarily used as guardians protecting treasures and important locations.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fists","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":77,"max":77},"mp":{"value":18,"max":18}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Semi-Transparent State","description":"This monster is naturally semi-transparent. The monster does not create shielding even when on the battlefield. Additionally, characters in different areas (Simplified Combat) or coordinates more than 10m away (Standard/Advanced Combat) cannot detect this monster.\nIt glows when its attack succeeds an Accuracy check, fails an Evasion check, or when its HP or MP is reduced by 1 or more points. This effect is nullified for the next 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"◯ Invisible Assassin / 16 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"When approaching this monster's hiding spot, you must perform a Danger Sense check with Target Number 16. If you fail, you'll receive a surprise attack from this monster (see CR I, p. 144)."},{"title":"►Double Attack","description":"Performs a double attack on 1 character target using both fists."},{"title":"►Burst Light / 9 (16) / Willpower / Half","description":"Emits an intense light with &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and deals Energy magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius)/5.&quot; If the monster was semi-transparent immediately before using this ability, the damage is 2d+10 points; otherwise, it's 2d+5 points.\nUsing this ability consumes 6 MP. This ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Black Stone (10G/Black B)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Clear Jewel (200G/Gold Red A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Shining Stone (2,000G/Gold Black S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghost Servant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sFQ7S2tkQMCFHQGB","name":"Ghost Curtain","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghost-curtain","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Sky","reputation":16,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/10 (Floating)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CO","description":"The Ghost Curtain is a fabric-like Construct that was created during the Magic Civilization Period. It moves by hanging down and floating in the air.\n\nThis Construct serves as a trap or a guard. Normally, it is invisible and remains vigilant of its surroundings. However, if something approaches within a 10-meter range or if it is attacked, it immediately engages in combat. During combat, it either emits a dazzling light that burns its surroundings, or clenches a part of its body like a fist and strikes the enemy.\n\nWhen the Ghost Curtain comes into contact with another person or experiences interference, it emits light in various ways depending on its strength and type. It is said that during the Magic Civilization Period, the wizard-king Lal, who lived in the rock country of Recode Floating Rocks Country, would float this construct in the air and enjoy the sight of it emitting light when birds and other creatures accidentally swooped down on it. When Recode was attacked, they were said to have released as much as they could into the sky as an air defense force.\n\nAlthough most of the Ghost Curtains were destroyed in the battle when Recode exploded, a few remain floating and invisible. The Cyrecode Council (see CO) has a policy of preserving them as a tourist resource if they are found at a safe distance from the environment. However, if they are found near a star or gondola cable, adventurers are to remove them.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Strike","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":62,"max":62},"mp":{"value":23,"max":23}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Conditional Invisibility","description":"This monster is usually invisible (see CR II, p. 69). It emits light when it successfully passes its Accuracy check, fails its Evasion check, or loses 1 point of HP or MP. After emitting light, the monster becomes visible for the next 10 seconds (1 round).\nThe color and strength of the emitted light depend on various factors such as the type of attack, whether HP or MP was damaged, and so on (up to the GM)."},{"title":"◯ Invisible Assassin / 18 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"If a character approaches a location where this monster is lurking, they need to make a Danger Sense check with target number 18. If they fail, they will be taken by surprise by this monster."},{"title":"► Burst Light / 8 (15) / Willpower / Half","description":"The ability &quot;Range: Caster&quot; emits a burst of light and deals energy magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot;. The damage inflicted is &quot;2d+10&quot; if the monster was invisible just before using this ability, and &quot;2d+4&quot; points otherwise. This ability costs 6 MP and cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Black Cloth (5G/-)"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Transparent Cloth (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Glowing Cloth (1,500G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghost Curtain","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sTz2QOx0PhMKoFIA","name":"Heroic Avatar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:heroic-avatar","level":11,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement) p. 138","description":"This is a phantom entity created by a powerful magic sword in the image of the hero who once wielded it. Although it doesn't match the original hero's full potential, it can freely wield most of its power. Its abilities vary greatly depending on which hero's phantom it embodies.\n\nIt is said that the magic sword tests those who seek to claim it by making them fight against this phantom entity to prove their worthiness. This monster is based on a magic warrior who played a crucial role in a great battle against Barbarous.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":87,"max":87},"mp":{"value":51,"max":51}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"△Hero's Acceleration","description":"Automatically gain the effect of the Spiritualism Magic spell [ Haste ]. Additionally, movement in the first round is limited to Limited Move.\nThis effect is treated as a magic effect with a Success Value of 21."},{"title":"🗨Mana Strike = +14 damage","description":"Increases damage by +14 points. As a risk, it incurs a -2 penalty to Fortitude and Willpower."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"►Magic (1 system) 11 level / Magic Power 14 (21)","description":"Has acquired any one Wizard-Type Class (if not specified, assume Truespeech Magic ) at level 11."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Hero's Mark (10,000G/Gold White SS)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Well-Kept Weapon (4,000G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Heroic Avatar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"toqghqTVWvsNVYlJ","name":"Ghast Cavalry","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast-cavalry","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla p. 132","description":"In the Ursyla region during the late Magic Civilization Period, there were Ghast cavalry units operated by Humanoids. Though created as a combination of horse and jockey, their bodies were completely integrated into one unit and could not be separated. While they possessed high combat capability, records show they were unable to execute complex tactical operations and were utilized purely as basic combat units.\n\nThe &quot;Control Stone&quot; was a magical instrument incorporated to enable such Ghasts with multiple movement sections to function without malfunction. Although its manufacturing method has been lost to time, research continues. Through this research, technology for implementing very simple commands has emerged. Centered in the Haroon Magical Research Kingdom, expensive mechanical toys with these stones embedded in dolls and stuffed animals are sold as luxury items for wealthy children.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon (Rider)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":46,"max":46},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hooves (Horse)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Horse","description":""},{"title":"◯ Downswing","description":"Adds +2 points of damage to the Rider section. This ability is lost if the Horse section's HP falls below 0."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Height impedes attacks. The Rider section gains a +4 bonus modifier to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect is lost if the Horse section's HP falls below 0."},{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If the Horse section's HP falls to &quot;0&quot; or below, no Control Stone loot can be obtained."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Control Stone (1,100G/Gold White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Dense Magic Jewel (700G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast Cavalry","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"twQfu2NlxDe1sf3l","name":"Maid Blob","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:maid-blob","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Procelsia, a Secret History (2.0 sourcebook), p. 168","description":"A Maid Blob is one of a series of jellied constructs that went haywire, Blobs , which in this case was made to take the form of a human woman. It has some intelligence and can obey orders.\n\nLike a Blob, it attacks the target by engulfing it in its body, but it does this by working on the target's psyche and trying to manipulate the mind to prevent escape.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Smash","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":0,"hp":{"value":65,"max":65},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Engulf / 10 (15) / Willpower / Negates","description":"If a Smash attack hits, the Maid Blob will put the target to sleep and then engulf the target into its body. The target is comatose and suffers 2d+1 magic damage at the end of each of the monster's turns.\nAn engulfed target can only perform one Willpower Check on its turn, and if it succeeds, it wakes up and escapes. After this check, the target's turn ends immediately, regardless of the result."},{"title":"◯ Soft Body","description":"Bludgeoning weapons treat the Defense of Blob section as 5 points higher. Also, Throw or similar attacks deal no damage and have no effect."},{"title":"◯ Acidic Body","description":"Anyone who attacks or receives an attack from a Blob will have their weapon or armor dissolve into nothing after 24 hours. This can be avoided by washing the affected weapon or armor with alcohol or wine within that 24 hours."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If Maid Blob is defeated while another character is in its body because of the [ ◯ Engulf], you will get a Jelly-like Heart. Otherwise, you will get a Jelly-like Material as loot."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Jelly-like Material (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Jelly-like Heart (300G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Mini-Blob (1,500G/Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Maid Blob","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uCDYWjHPMnjvo5EJ","name":"Sand Ghast","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sand-ghast","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Deserts","reputation":9,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 126","description":"This construct is found in the Kaslot Desert of the Burlight Region and is composed of sand. It has the size and shape of a Humanoid, but its face is flat and lacks any details.\n\nIt is believed that the abandoned magical nucleus, originally created for a Golem during the Magic Civilization Period, spontaneously generated power and gathered surrounding sand to bring this Construct to life.\n\nThe Construct is aggressive and will attack anyone who approaches it. This aggressive behavior may be attributed to the Golem's original purpose, which was likely for combat, either in a defensive or offensive role.\n\nAt the center of this Construct is the nucleus which gives it life. This nucleus can be purchased at a high price and used as a material for crafting Sand Armor (see Natural History of Burlight p. 42).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":22,"max":22},"mp":{"value":13,"max":13}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Sand Body","description":"It does not receive a critical hit from any attack that deals physical damage."},{"title":"◯Core Regeneration = 3 points","description":"At the end of its turn, it regains 3 points of HP. This ability is lost if its HP is 0 or less or the Sand Ghast receives magic damage which is dealt with a critical hit."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"The Loot item &quot;Regenerative Nucleus&quot; cannot be obtained from Sand Ghasts who have suffered magical damage that was caused by a critical hit during combat."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Regenerative Nucleus (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sand Ghast","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uaj1ryS9LHc1Q3Jx","name":"Alert Gramophone","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:alert-gramophone","level":9,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR II p. 381","description":"This is a sound device made in the Magic Civilization Period to repel intruders. A large horn is mounted on the top of the pedestal-like body, and it has four short legs for moving and two long, thin hands for operating the device on the top.\n\nWhen the monster detects an intruder in the house, it lures them with its spellsongs and draws them into a trap. After that, the monster attacks the intruder with its arms and spellsongs.\n\nThe type of spellsong that can be played is specified at the time of creation, and it seems that some of them play other spellsongs rather than [Curiosity].","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arm","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":79,"max":79},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"The monster can perform two Major Actions in one round. However, one must be a melee attack with Arm, and the other must be either a [ ► Basic Spellsongs] [ ► Special Spellsong] or [ ► Finale]."},{"title":"► Basic Spellsongs 5 Level/12 (19)/All areas (50m radius)","description":""},{"title":"► Special Spellsong [ Curiosity ]/12 (19)/All areas (50m radius)","description":"Plays spellsong [ Curiosity ]. This unique skill can only be used if the current value of this monster's HP is at least half of the maximum value (rounded up)."},{"title":"► [Finale: Screaming Snake-pit Symphony]/12 (19)/Willpower/Half","description":"Uses [ Finale: Screaming Snake-pit Symphony ] within &quot;Range: 2 (50m)&quot; to deal 2d+10 Curse magic damage to up to 3 targets.\nThis unique skill can only be used if the current value of this monster's HP is less than half of the maximum value (rounded up)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Plain Trumpet (50G/Black White B)"},{"roll":"10 - 13","loot":"Exquisite Horn (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"14+","loot":"Luxury Horn (5,800G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Alert Gramophone","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"wFyspK3btR0JB0Bw","name":"Insomnia Beat","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:insomnia-beat","level":10,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Graves, Ruins, Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"-/11 (Floating)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"AB, p. 106","description":"This is a heart-tormenting type of Construct, considered a failed creation produced during research into magical items that resurrect living beings. This monster carves out music in time with its own beating, but it produces discordant sounds that cause the dead to rise as Undead and disturb the physical condition of the living.\n\nOnce it appears, it moves accompanied by Undead, and if not dealt with quickly, many people will become living dead.\n\nThe sound when these Undead march under the control of this Construct is likened to irregular heartbeats.\n\nThere have been sightings within the Shallow Abysses, where it is said that its pulsations (distortedly) receive the feelings of those wishing to resurrect their loved ones, causing it to dance even more violently.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"12(19)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":12,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Limited 2 Actions","description":"It can perform 2 Major Actions in 1 round. However, these are limited to a combination where one action must be a melee attack using Slam, and the other must be either [►Basic Spellsongs], [►Special Spellsong], or [►Finale]."},{"title":"►Basic Spellsongs 10 Level / 13 (20) / All Areas (50m radius)","description":"The list of usable Spellsongs includes those from page 332 of CR II, plus [ Dare ] (see CR III, p. 177).\nAlternatively, refer to page 70 of ML."},{"title":"►Special Spellsong [Reverse Requiem] / 13 (20) / All Areas (50m radius)","description":"This ability cannot be used unless Basic Spellsongs were used in previous turns. Uses Spellsong [Reverse Requiem]. This Spellsong is &quot;Type: Psychic&quot; and &quot;Resistance: Negates.&quot; Targets who fail their Willpower check receive a -2 penalty to all skill checks."},{"title":"◯Distorted Heartbeat","description":"The [►Basic Spellsongs] and [►Special Spellsong] used by this monster have the following characteristics:\nThe &quot;Type&quot; becomes &quot;None.&quot; When the target is classified as &quot;Undead&quot;, &quot;Resistance: Can't&quot; applies, and the positive/negative effects are reversed (for example, with [Ballad], it changes to a +1 bonus to Evasion checks)."},{"title":"►[Finale: Screaming Snake-pit Symphony] / 13 (20) / Willpower / Half","description":"With &quot;Range: 2 (50m)&quot;, it uses [ Finale: Screaming Snake-pit Symphony ] to deal 2d+11 points of Curse magic damage to up to 3 targets.\nThis ability can only be used when this monster's current HP is at or below half (rounded up) of its maximum value."},{"title":"►[Finale: Roar of the Water Dragon] / 13 (20) / Willpower / Half (Shallow)","description":"With &quot;Range: 2 (50m)&quot;, it uses [ Finale: Roar of the Water Dragon ] to deal 2d+13 points of Water/Ice and Lightning magical damage to up to 5 targets.\nThis ability can only be used when this monster is within a Shallow Abyss and its current HP is at or below one-fourth (rounded up) of its maximum value."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Weak Heart (270G/Red A)"},{"roll":"10 - 12","loot":"Loud Heart (2,770G/Gold Red S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Beating Heart (7,700G/Gold Red S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Insomnia Beat","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"x3q2uuwvrMxPXIXH","name":"Gargoyle","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gargoyle","level":3,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":9,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15/30 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 421","description":"A variety of golem with both claws and wings, a Gargoyle is a beast of stone animated by long-lost magic. Gargoyles were famous guardians of the Magic Civilization period, and most seen today are still following instructions given to them from that time. While Gargoyles seem to act as living beings, they can choose to camouflage themselves as stone, taking advantage of unaware and careless adventurers.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Claws","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":26,"max":26},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mimicry/12/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It mimics a stone statue. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If the character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 12, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144).\nMimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act. This monster can be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Sharp Stone (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Enchanted Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gargoyle","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"x6h15xkob7Ddc3Gy","name":"Corrupt Caterpillar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:corrupt-caterpillar","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10 (Crawling)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement) p. 137","description":"This Construct resembles a yellowish-green caterpillar coated in dark, putrid mucus. Its body features countless small warts that continuously generate tiny replicas of itself. Though these copies lack significant combat prowess, they produce threads that blanket their environment in fungi. The fungi infiltrate and multiply within living organisms' organs, particularly their respiratory systems. As a result, any territory inhabited by Corrupt Caterpillars becomes overwhelmed with fungal growth, rendering it lethal to Humanoids and all other living beings.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Fungal Spread / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Scatters fungal spores from protrusions all over its body. Within &quot;Range/Area: Caster&quot;, deals 2d+5 points of magic damage to targets in &quot;1 area (5m radius) / 15&quot;. Additionally, for 7 days, two randomly determined ability scores decrease by 3 points. This effect stacks until any ability score reaches 0 (when failing resistance, two ability scores are randomly determined and decreased).\nBoth the damage and ability score reduction are treated as Disease effects.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"►Proliferation","description":"Creates an identical entity from protrusions all over its body. At the end of the round, 1 x Corrupt Caterpillar appears at the same coordinates as the monster that used this ability. The newly appeared Corrupt Caterpillar acts independently from the next round.\nThe HP of the newly appearing Character is equal to half (rounded up) of this monster's current HP. Using this ability reduces the current HP to half (rounded up). This ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Mycelium Bundle (100G/Red A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Black Mushroom Bed (600G/-)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Corrupt Caterpillar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xVZUvG4mm1xWUu6V","name":"Familiars II","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:familiars-ii","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Shared with Caster","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":0,"weakPoint":"None","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"5 (4 Legs)/10 (Swimming)","fortitude":"-","willpower":"-","source":"CR I p. 434","description":"This is data for Advanced Familiars, which can be summoned with the Truespeech Magic spell [ Familiar II ].\n\nSee also: Common Abilities of Advanced Familiars .","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tongue","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":20,"max":20}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Frog's Body","description":"The frog can move underwater. Its mobility is equal to that of a normal frog."},{"title":"Spider","description":"Initiative: 16\nMovement Speed: 7 (Many Legs)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nBite | 9 (16) | 2d+8 | | 9 (16) | 6 | | - | 15 |"},{"title":"◯Spider's Body","description":"The spider can move freely on walls and ceilings. While sticking to the ceiling, it will not be targeted by a wide range of effects unless the enemy specifically targets the Familiar. Its mobility is equal to a recluse spider."},{"title":"Bird","description":"Initiative: 18\nMovement Speed: -/30 (Flying)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nBeak | 10 (17) | 2d+8 | | 10 (17) | 6 | | - | 15 |"},{"title":"◯Bird's Body","description":"Capable of flight. Physical ability is that of a normal bird."},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Bird Familiar receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"Cat","description":"Initiative: 18\nMovement Speed: 12 (4 Legs)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nClaws | 10 (17) | 2d+8 | | 10 (17) | 7 | | - | 15 |"},{"title":"◯Cat's Body","description":"Can pass through narrow gaps, etc. Physical ability is the same as an ordinary housecat."},{"title":"◯Gives Darkvision","description":"Shares its Darkvision with its Master."},{"title":"Snake","description":"Initiative: 16\nMovement Speed: 10 (Slithering)\nFighting Style | Accuracy | Damage | | Evasion | Defense | | HP | MP |\nBite | 10 (17) | 2d+8 | | 11 (18) | 7 | | - | 15 |"},{"title":"◯Snake's Body","description":"The snake can pass through extremely narrow spaces. Its physical ability is equal to that of the normal snake."},{"title":"◯Toxic Tooth","description":"When a Snake Familiar makes a melee attack and hits, it automatically deals 1 Poison magic damage to the target of the melee attack. This ability only works if the Familiar is in Touch range with the Master.\n<div"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Familiars II","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yfLFbzFmV1hMdgaD","name":"Terror Familiar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:terror-familiar","level":7,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Shared with Caster","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Daemonic, Arcana","habitat":"Various, Shallows","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"-","willpower":"-","source":"AB, p. 104","description":"The Terror Familiar is a higher-level familiar than the Familiar from Beyond , created by Daemons of level 11 or higher who use Truespeech Magic and their own blood to craft this familiar. It inherits and enhances the abilities of the Familiar from Beyond. The [◯Shared Visibility] is no longer limited to the Shallow Abysses. Like its predecessor, it will sacrifice itself to protect its master, though this trait has become even more dangerous.\n\nWhile its form is modeled after a Terror Beast , it does not instill fear merely by its appearance and lacks the ability to use Divine Magic.\n\nWithin a Shallow, it manifests a troublesome HP regeneration ability.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"&#32;","defense":10,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Daemon Familiar","description":"The following abilities are common to these familiars. For individual details, see CR I, p. 432, ML. p. 235.\n[◯Poison Immunity], [◯Disease Immunity], [◯Psychic Immunity], [◯Can be Detected], [◯Familiar Contract], [◯Familiars Knowledge = Sorcerers], [◯Shared MP], [◯Resistance Sharing], and [◯Senses Sharing]"},{"title":"◯Free Will","description":"Unlike regular Familiars ([◯Will-less]), Terror Familiars possess their own will. They are capable of communication through Arcana and Daemonic. However, they maintain unwavering loyalty to their master and will never take actions that would constitute betrayal."},{"title":"◯Shared Visibility","description":"The caster can use this monster's line of sight to cast spells. However, the point of origin for spell casting is always the caster. When considering range distance, it must be calculated from the caster's position, and spells with &quot;Area: Shot &quot; or &quot;Area: Line &quot; are fired from the caster.\nWhen casting spells from the familiar's viewpoint as a Major Action, both the master and this monster complete their Major Actions. When cast as a Minor Action, both are considered to have performed Minor Actions."},{"title":"►Invisibility","description":"This effect requires 5 MP points to use.\nAgainst characters with &quot;Perception: Five Senses&quot; or &quot;Perception: Mechanical&quot;, it becomes invisible . Characters with &quot;Perception: Magic&quot; can still detect its presence.\nInvisibility is maintained unless it performs a Full Move or Major Action, in which case it automatically ends immediately after."},{"title":"►Desperate Self-Destruct II / Can't","description":"This effect can only be used when its current HP is at or below one-fourth (rounded up) of its maximum HP.\nMakes a special attack against &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5&quot; with &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot; and self-destructs. Deals 2d+15 points of Fire magic damage to the target. When using this effect, Terror Familiar's HP automatically becomes &quot;0&quot; and it is destroyed."},{"title":"◯Regeneration = 7 points (Shallow)","description":"At the end of its turn, HP recovers by 7 points. This effect only appears when this monster is inside a Shallow Abyss.\nWhen HP drops to 0 or below, this ability is lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Crystallized Daemon's Blood (800G/Red A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Terror Familiar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yh5wn3xe8iVlMzFS","name":"Junkwalker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:junkwalker","level":6,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"KF","description":"This construct is a pile of junk that has gained consciousness. Its body is composed entirely of debris, garbage, pieces of wood, and stone, and it changes shape as it moves. In rare cases, special objects or rare ores may be mixed in with its body. When it moves violently, it self-destructs and scatters junk around itself.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fists (Right)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":64,"max":64},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Fists (Left)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":64,"max":64},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Right / Left","description":""},{"title":"◯ Junk Self-destruction/Can't","description":"Its body self-destructs.\nImmediately after both the Right and Left sections' body have finished their turns, one of the randomly selected sections receives 1d+2 fixed damage to its HP, and all other characters in the same area (area, coordinates) except the character itself receive double that amount of physical damage.\nThis ability is lost when the HP of any section falls to 0 or less."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Junkwalker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zCClf6x7JmiJVETU","name":"Ghast Lurker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ghast-lurker","level":2,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":5,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.148","description":"This is a slightly grown-up Ghast , about the size of an adult Human, otherwise the same as a Ghast.\n\nIn rare cases, there are Ghast Lurkers that act of their own volition.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Smash","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":18,"max":18},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Construct HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ghast Lurker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zDLKnDKdqNwE5jyN","name":"Abyss Servant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-servant","level":5,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"8(15)","willpower":"7(14)","source":"AB, p. 103","description":"This is a Stone Servant created with an embedded Abyss Shard. While enhanced by the Abyss Shard, it also contains inherent instability.\n\nCreated by the inhabitants of the Shallow Abyss, it primarily appears and provides support alongside the guardians who protect the Abyss Core.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Knowledge = Conjurer class","description":"Those with the Conjurer class automatically succeed on Monster Knowledge checks against this monster. To know its weak point, the original weakness value is required."},{"title":"◯Stone Body","description":"Does not receive critical hits from edged weapons or magic except Energy type."},{"title":"◯Double Attack","description":"Can attack one target twice with both fists."},{"title":"◯Self-Harming Painful Strike","description":"If the result of 2d for damage determination is 9 or higher, increase damage by 5 points. Simultaneously receives 5 points of fixed damage to own HP."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 12","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Servant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zRfr4EACRsu9uBjf","name":"Abyss Golem","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:abyss-golem","level":8,"monsterType":"Construct","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":14,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Energy type damage +3 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"10/-","fortitude":"11(18)","willpower":"11(18)","source":"AB, p. 105","description":"This is a Rock Golem created with an embedded Abyss Shard. While it has been enhanced by the Abyss Shard, it also contains inherent instability as a result.\n\nCreated by the inhabitants of the Shallow Abyss, it primarily appears and provides support alongside the guardians who protect the Abyss Core.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist (Right Half)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"&#32;","defense":7,"hp":{"value":12,"max":12},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Fist (Left Half)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"&#32;","defense":7,"hp":{"value":12,"max":12},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Knowledge = Conjurer class","description":"Those with the Conjurer class automatically succeed on Monster Knowledge checks against this monster. To know its weak point, the original weakness value is required."},{"title":"◯Rock Body","description":"The Abyss Golem is immune to criticals from edged weapons and all non-Energy-type Magic damage."},{"title":"🗨Aimed Attack","description":"An Abyss Golem gains a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks, but its own damage is reduced by -4."},{"title":"◯Self-Harming Painful Strike","description":"If the result of 2d for damage determination is 9 or higher, increase damage by 5 points. Simultaneously receives 5 points of fixed damage to own HP."},{"title":"◯Unstable Coordination","description":"This effect only occurs when both Right Body and Left Body sections are intact. Roll 1d at the start of its turn.\nOn 1-3: Right Body and Left Body sections must target different characters for melee attacks. Both sections must declare [🗨Aimed Attack]. If there is only one character available as a melee attack target, this effect does not occur.\nOn 4-6: Right Body and Left Body sections must target the same character for melee attacks. There are no restrictions on the first acting section's attack, but the section acting later must follow this rule: &quot;If the first section's attack missed, declare [🗨Aimed Attack]; if it hit, make an attack without declaration.&quot;"},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal a Construct's HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Construct's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Constructs can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Magical Stone (250G/Gold A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Mithril (2,600G/Gold S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Abyss Golem","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}